    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "TIT",
      "chapter": 3,
      "chapter_usfm": "TIT.3",
      "version_id": 2692,
      "version_abbr": "NASB2020",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Remind them to be subject to rulers, to authorities, to be obedient, to be ready for every good deed,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "to slander no one, not to be contentious, to be gentle, showing every consideration for all people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For we too were once foolish, disobedient, deceived, enslaved to various lusts and pleasures, spending our life in malice and envy, hateful, hating one another."
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But when the kindness of God our Savior and His love for mankind appeared,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "He saved us, not on the basis of deeds which we did in righteousness, but in accordance with His mercy, by the washing of regeneration and renewing by the Holy Spirit,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "whom He richly poured out upon us through Jesus Christ our Savior,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "so that being justified by His grace we would be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "This statement is trustworthy; and concerning these things I want you to speak confidently, so that those who have believed God will be careful to engage in good deeds. These things are good and beneficial for people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But avoid foolish controversies and genealogies and strife and disputes about the Law, for they are useless and worthless."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Reject a divisive person after a first and second warning,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "knowing that such a person has deviated from what is right and is sinning, being self-condemned."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "When I send Artemas or Tychicus to you, make every effort to come to me at Nicopolis, for I have decided to spend the winter there."
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Diligently help Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their way so that nothing is lacking for them."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Our people must also learn to engage in good deeds to meet pressing needs, so that they will not be unproductive."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "TIT.3.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "All who are with me greet you. Greet those who love us in the faith. Grace be with you all."
        }
      ],
